# ez-comfy-stack operator environment - template for the repo-root env file.
#
# What this is: every host-side knob ./scripts/manage.sh and docker compose
#   read for the one-box US-safe studio. ./scripts/manage.sh setup copies this
#   file to the repo-root env file; scripts/lib/common.sh load_dotenv then
#   exports each uncommented KEY=value line (a value already in your shell
#   wins, so an export beats what is written here).
# Copy and edit: ./scripts/manage.sh setup   (or, by hand: cp it to .env)
# Never commit the real file: the real one and .env.local are gitignored and
#   this example is the only tracked copy, so keep tokens and hostnames out.
# Layout: sections are the `# ---` banners below and keys inside a section run
#   most-important-first. A commented key already holds the value shown (the
#   code default); uncomment it only to change that value.
# Long-form docs: docs/getting-started.mdx and
#   docs/reference/config-and-schemas.mdx. Multi-Spark: last section.

# --- Required paths -------------------------------------------------------

# MODELS_DIR - host directory bind-mounted read-write at /models; the single
#   shared weights cache for every download-* pack (compose:101).
# Set: keep the default on a dedicated Spark - manage.sh, doctor, and the docs
#   all assume it, and tests/bats/safety.bats pins it. It must be writable by
#   your user (setup creates it):
#     sudo mkdir -p /mnt/models && sudo chown "$USER:$USER" /mnt/models
#   Use MODELS_DIR=$HOME/models for a throwaway box. Keep it off tmpfs: packs
#   run to tens of GB.
MODELS_DIR=/mnt/models

# COMFY_OUTPUT_DIR - host directory for generated PNG/MP4 plus the Comfy user/,
#   input/ and custom-nodes-user trees (compose:104-111). Inside the container
#   the code sees /outputs, not this host path (compose:94).
# Set: keep the default unless the weights cache needs its own disk; then point
#   both at real mounts and create them the same way:
#     sudo mkdir -p /mnt/comfy-output && sudo chown "$USER:$USER" /mnt/comfy-output
COMFY_OUTPUT_DIR=/mnt/comfy-output

# HOST_UID / HOST_GID - owner stamped on directories the container creates as
#   root inside those bind mounts (docker/install-comfy/common.sh:250
#   layout_host_uid_gid; compose:96-97).
# Set: leave commented. ./scripts/manage.sh start already exports both from
#   `id -u` / `id -g` (scripts/lib/compose.sh:602-603), so you only need them
#   for a raw `docker compose` run, or when /models is owned by another uid.
# HOST_UID=
# HOST_GID=

# --- Ports and memory -----------------------------------------------------

# COMFY_PORT - host port published to the container's 8188 (compose:51);
#   manage.sh status/start/verify probe it (scripts/lib/compose.sh:245).
# Set: 8188 unless something else on the Spark owns it. The mapping is the
#   only exposure - reach the UI from the LAN through your own proxy.
COMFY_PORT=8188

# STUDIO_UI_PORT - host port for the optional studio-ui jobstore board, which
#   runs only under the compose "studio-ui" profile (compose:141).
# Set: 8190 unless taken; irrelevant until you start that profile.
# STUDIO_UI_PORT=8190

# MEM_LIMIT / MEM_RESERVATION - docker mem_limit / mem_reservation for the
#   unified us-safe-studio container (compose:129-130; defaults restated in
#   scripts/lib/compose.sh:596-597 and scripts/lib/safety.sh:34).
# Set: together, and leave 10-20 GB of the 128 GB GB10 for SSH/OS - doctor
#   warns when MEM_LIMIT + MIN_HOST_FREE_GIB exceeds 128 (safety.sh:271). Lower
#   both on a smaller host; never raise MEM_LIMIT past what you can spare.
MEM_LIMIT=90g
MEM_RESERVATION=80g

# MIN_HOST_FREE_GIB - headroom preflight: refuse manage.sh start below this
#   much free host RAM (scripts/lib/safety.sh:32).
# Set: 28 is the SSH-safe floor for a 128 GB Spark running the 90g container.
#   Do not raise it much - start fails closed - and do not lower it to squeeze
#   in a video job; that is what the occupancy XOR gate exists for.
MIN_HOST_FREE_GIB=28

# MIN_DISK_FREE_GIB - the same gate for free disk on the MODELS_DIR path
#   (scripts/lib/safety.sh:33).
# Set: 40 is enough for the smallest pack. Raise it (say 200) if you want
#   doctor/start to stop you before a Wan/LTX pull can fill the disk.
# MIN_DISK_FREE_GIB=40

# --- Image and build ------------------------------------------------------

# App image (Comfy + torch + node packs; never weights). Pull comes from GHCR.
# EZ_COMFY_IMAGE - image ref used for run and as local build cache. Unset,
#   manage.sh picks the tag from the current git branch
#   (scripts/lib/compose.sh:499-505):
#     main         -> ghcr.io/toxicoder/ez-comfy:us-safe-studio
#     development  -> ghcr.io/toxicoder/ez-comfy:us-safe-studio-development
#     feature/*    -> ghcr.io/toxicoder/ez-comfy:us-safe-studio-development
# Set: leave commented so the branch decides. Pin an explicit tag only to hold
#   a box on a known build.
# EZ_COMFY_IMAGE=ghcr.io/toxicoder/ez-comfy:us-safe-studio-development

# LAB_STACK_FORCE_BUILD / LAB_STACK_SKIP_PULL - start path: 1 = build the
#   Dockerfile locally (scripts/lib/compose.sh:615) / 1 = never docker pull
#   (scripts/lib/compose.sh:522). Both default 0 = pull GHCR.
# Set: 1 only for a Dockerfile change. The ops scripts (entrypoint, install,
#   patch_*.py) are bind-mounted, so editing them needs no rebuild; rebuild
#   only to rebake /opt/comfy-prebuilt (torch/comfy/nodes phases).
# LAB_STACK_FORCE_BUILD=1
# LAB_STACK_SKIP_PULL=1

# LAB_FORCE_COLD_INSTALL - 1 = ignore the baked /opt/comfy-prebuilt and pip
#   install at runtime (docker/entrypoint.sh:1667).
# Set: 0 unless you are debugging the install phases; 1 costs minutes per boot.
# LAB_FORCE_COLD_INSTALL=1

# EZ_COMFY_PREBUILD - build arg: 1 = bake Comfy+torch into the image, 0 = thin
#   image that pip-installs on first boot (compose:27; docker/Dockerfile:81).
# Set: 1 (default). 0 is for image-size experiments.
# EZ_COMFY_PREBUILD=1

# CUDA images - one place for both. CUDA_BASE_IMAGE is the multi-stage
#   builder (docker/Dockerfile:40) and CUDA_RUNTIME_IMAGE the final stage
#   (docker/Dockerfile:159); both default to the same wheels-only runtime tag,
#   no nvcc and no NGC login (compose:24-25).
# Set: leave both commented for the normal path. Uncomment CUDA_BASE_IMAGE with
#   a devel tag only when you compile CUDA extensions locally:
#     CUDA_BASE_IMAGE=nvidia/cuda:13.0.0-devel-ubuntu24.04
#   After `docker login nvcr.io` you can take both from NGC instead:
#     CUDA_BASE_IMAGE=nvcr.io/nvidia/cuda:13.0.0-runtime-ubuntu24.04
#     CUDA_RUNTIME_IMAGE=nvcr.io/nvidia/cuda:13.0.0-runtime-ubuntu24.04
# CUDA_BASE_IMAGE=nvidia/cuda:13.0.0-runtime-ubuntu24.04
# CUDA_RUNTIME_IMAGE=nvidia/cuda:13.0.0-runtime-ubuntu24.04

# TORCH_VERSION / TORCH_INDEX_URL - the validated pins for the bake
#   (compose:29-30).
# Set: leave commented to take the repo's tested pin; set a pair to roll back,
#   or set empty to float deliberately.
# TORCH_VERSION=2.14.1
# TORCH_INDEX_URL=https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu130

# ComfyUI and node pack refs - build args (compose:31-38); the four that the
#   runtime volume also pins are mirrored into the container env for the
#   stamp-checked refresh (compose:75-78).
# Set: leave commented - these are the tested pins. Bump one only when you are
#   deliberately chasing an upstream fix, then restart so the volume refresh
#   sees the new ref. COMFYUI_VHS_REF empty means VideoHelperSuite main, which
#   the LTX lab needs for VHS_VideoCombine.
# COMFYUI_REF=v0.43.0
# COMFYUI_MANAGER_REF=4.2.2
# COMFYUI_NUNCHAKU_NODE_REF=v1.2.1
# COMFYUI_VHS_REF=
# COMFYUI_OPENCUT_REF=0.5.0
# COMFYUI_MAGCACHE_REF=47bdd2aca97e568087c4e92d2d2f0426bdce7a37
# COMFYUI_LTX_DIRECTOR_REF=a3c809c8b593a74c2ddcd6c1f83ad85ebebe3c64

# LAB_ENABLE_LTX_DIRECTOR - 1 = clone the GPL LTX Director pack into the Comfy
#   volume at the pin above (docker/install-comfy/phase-nodes.sh:496).
# Set: 0 (default) keeps the shipped graph set permissive-licensed; 1 only if
#   you accept the GPL pack.
# LAB_ENABLE_LTX_DIRECTOR=1

# --- Prompt-enhance LLM ---------------------------------------------------

# On-box prompt enhance: a CPU llama.cpp GGUF (custom_nodes/ez_prompt_enhance)
#   that download-models pulls. Defaults live once, in
#   docker/docker-compose.yml:65-71, and the client constants agree with them
#   (custom_nodes/ez_prompt_enhance/client.py:64-66).

# EZ_LLM_GGUF - which GGUF the enhancer loads (compose:65).
# Set: leave commented - the client probes comfy/llm and the HF snapshot dir on
#   its own, and setting this is the documented last resort (client.py:1040-1043).
# EZ_LLM_GGUF=/models/comfy/llm/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507-Q4_K_M.gguf

# EZ_LLM_N_THREADS - llama.cpp CPU threads (compose:66; client.py:814).
# Set: 8 default. Raise toward the 20 GB10 cores only when prompt enhance feels
#   slow and nothing heavy is running; the compose cpus cap is a separate limit.
# EZ_LLM_N_THREADS=8

# EZ_LLM_N_CTX - context length (compose:67; client.py:830, floor 512).
# Set: 4096 default covers a normal prompt; raise only for long style blocks.
# EZ_LLM_N_CTX=4096

# EZ_LLM_TIMEOUT_S - per-call generate timeout, model load included
#   (compose:68; client.py:798,911).
# Set: 180 default is sized for a cold CPU load. Lower it if you would rather
#   fall back to the canned prompt quickly.
# EZ_LLM_TIMEOUT_S=180

# EZ_LLM_N_GPU_LAYERS - layers offloaded to the GPU (compose:69; client.py:1025).
# Set: 0 = CPU. Occupancy already handles this - wan/ltx/trellis force CPU
#   (OOM-safe) and klein/llm/idle ngl the 4B automatically - so set it only to
#   force an offload yourself (99 = all layers).
# EZ_LLM_N_GPU_LAYERS=0

# EZ_LLM_ALLOW_GPU - 0 = never touch the GPU whatever occupancy says
#   (client.py:1018).
# Set: 0 on a box that runs video jobs and has shown VRAM pressure; leave unset
#   to let occupancy decide.
# EZ_LLM_ALLOW_GPU=0

# EZ_LLM_UNLOAD - 1 = close the llama.cpp handle after each call, freeing RAM
#   but reloading the GGUF next time (compose:70; client.py:1090).
# Set: 1 only when the enhancer is the RAM hog between heavy jobs.
# EZ_LLM_UNLOAD=0

# Opt-in 35B writing desk (occupancy llm-desk): a separate llama-server, not
#   part of download-models. Operator CLI: ./scripts/manage.sh llm-sidecar.

# EZ_LLM_SIDECAR_HOST / EZ_LLM_SIDECAR_PORT / EZ_LLM_SIDECAR_CTX - bind, port
#   and context of that server (scripts/utilities/llm-sidecar.sh:40-42; the
#   port also passes into the container, compose:71).
# Set: defaults are right. Keep the bind on loopback - do not set 0.0.0.0.
#   Raise CTX only if you paste whole scripts into the desk.
# EZ_LLM_SIDECAR_HOST=127.0.0.1
# EZ_LLM_SIDECAR_PORT=30000
# EZ_LLM_SIDECAR_CTX=8192

# --- Optional models ------------------------------------------------------

# HF_TOKEN - Hugging Face read token: the only credential in this stack. It is
#   passed to the container at runtime and never baked into an image layer
#   (compose:63,45). Needed for the gated FLUX / LTX-2.5 weights; optional if
#   you are already logged in as this user.
# Set: a fine-grained read token scoped to the gated repos. NEVER commit the
#   real file, and never paste a token into a PR, log, or bug report.
# HF_TOKEN=

# EZ_PERSON_MASK / EZ_PERSON_MASK_PATH - opt-in Cubic block-world person mask
#   (BSD-3 DeepLabV3 ResNet50, ~165 MB;
#   custom_nodes/ez_image/person_mask.py:73). Not part of download-models: the
#   first stills/background-swap Cubic Queue downloads it into
#   ${MODELS_DIR}/comfy/ez-person/, and canvas Check models shows the same curl
#   command. Without it the swap keeps people photoreal (photo-anchored
#   rebuild) instead of erasing and pasting them.
# Set: leave both commented to use the mask as soon as it is downloaded. Set
#   EZ_PERSON_MASK=off to skip the paste (selects the people-kept cubic
#   rebuild). Point EZ_PERSON_MASK_PATH at the .pth only when it lives outside
#   comfy/ez-person.
# EZ_PERSON_MASK=off
# EZ_PERSON_MASK_PATH=/models/comfy/ez-person/deeplabv3_resnet50_coco-cd0a2569.pth

# --- Download bandwidth ---------------------------------------------------

# DOWNLOAD_LIMIT - throttle for manage.sh download-models
#   (scripts/manage.sh:56):
#     auto  - duration HTTP probe (then Ookla / speedtest-cli), then 85% of measured Mbps
#     off   - no throttle (not recommended over remote SSH)
#     <N>   - fixed Mbps, e.g. 50
# Set: auto. Use a fixed number on a shared link that needs a hard cap; off
#   only on a wired box you sit in front of. Auto results cache 24h per host
#   (not in MODELS_DIR); remeasure with
#   ./scripts/manage.sh download-limit status --refresh
DOWNLOAD_LIMIT=auto

# DOWNLOAD_LIMIT_FALLBACK - Mbps used when every auto probe fails
#   (scripts/utilities/download-limit.sh:74).
# Set: a rate your link can always sustain, so a flaky probe can neither
#   starve nor flood the download.
DOWNLOAD_LIMIT_FALLBACK=50

# DOWNLOAD_LIMIT_CACHE_TTL_SEC - age limit for the host speed cache in seconds
#   (scripts/utilities/download-limit.sh:70,86400 = 24h).
# Set: 86400 default; 0 = remeasure on every download (fluctuating link).
DOWNLOAD_LIMIT_CACHE_TTL_SEC=86400

# --- Progress and logging -------------------------------------------------

# Operator progress goes to stderr: bars and heartbeats on a TTY, periodic
#   newlines otherwise, so a captured log stays readable.

# EZ_COMFY_PROGRESS - default 1; 0 drops bars/heartbeats while log/warn/err
#   keep printing (scripts/lib/progress.sh:26).
# Set: 0 for cron or a log file you will grep later.
# EZ_COMFY_PROGRESS=0

# EZ_COMFY_PROGRESS_INTERVAL - heartbeat seconds for ffmpeg/blender/rsync/
#   docker (scripts/lib/progress.sh:50). Default 2.
# Set: 2 locally; 5-10 over a laggy SSH link.
# EZ_COMFY_PROGRESS_INTERVAL=2

# HF_PROGRESS / HF_PROGRESS_INTERVAL - disk-growth lines during Hugging Face
#   pulls and their tick in seconds (scripts/lib/common.sh:2116,1864).
#   Defaults 1 and 10.
# Set: HF_PROGRESS=0 to silence a chatty pull; raise the interval on a slow link.
# HF_PROGRESS=0
# HF_PROGRESS_INTERVAL=10

# EZ_COMFY_LOG_LEVEL - info|debug (scripts/lib/progress.sh:101). Default info.
# Set: debug (or LAB_DEBUG=1, which means the same thing) when filing a bug; it
#   dumps the download and traffic-shaping decisions.
# EZ_COMFY_LOG_LEVEL=debug

# NO_COLOR - any value disables ANSI escapes on stderr
#   (scripts/lib/common.sh:124; scripts/lib/progress.sh:37).
# Set: 1 when piping into a file or a pastebin.
# NO_COLOR=1

# --- Automation -----------------------------------------------------------

# For CI, cron, and scripts: the heavy-GPU confirm gate
# (scripts/lib/safety.sh) needs both keys to proceed without a TTY.

# LAB_STACK_FOLLOW - default 0: compose up -d then detach, so the stack
#   survives a dropped SSH session. 1 = manage.sh start stays in this shell
#   streaming logs until the UI port answers (scripts/lib/compose.sh:347).
# Set: 1 only while you watch a cold first boot in person.
# LAB_STACK_FOLLOW=1

# LAB_STACK_READY_TIMEOUT - seconds that follow waits for the UI port before
#   it gives up; it warns and leaves the container running
#   (scripts/lib/compose.sh:344). Default 2700 (45 min).
# Set: keep >= 2700 while a prebuilt miss can still trigger a torch install
#   (20+ min); lower it only when you want a fast CI failure.
# LAB_STACK_READY_TIMEOUT=2700

# LAB_NON_INTERACTIVE - 1 = never prompt (scripts/lib/common.sh:397).
# Set: 1 in CI. It fails closed unless LAB_CONFIRM_TOKEN is set too.
# LAB_NON_INTERACTIVE=1

# LAB_CONFIRM_TOKEN - the phrase the heavy confirm accepts with no TTY
#   (scripts/lib/safety.sh:65). It is not a credential: the interactive prompt
#   accepts the word yes.
# Set: exactly yes in the job that must not block.
# LAB_CONFIRM_TOKEN=yes

# --- Multi-Spark pointer --------------------------------------------------

# This file is the one-box studio profile: everything a single Spark needs and
#   nothing it does not. Independent Sparks (./scripts/utilities/spark-farm.sh
#   status / sync-models / dispatch) have their own profile in
#   config/spark-farm.example.env - copy that to config/spark-farm.env and
#   source it before the utility. It re-declares MODELS_DIR and
#   COMFY_OUTPUT_DIR on purpose, because the SSH/rsync side needs the same host
#   paths on every node; that is a deliberate split, not drift. Keep cluster
#   hostnames and fabric IPs out of this file and put them in the farm file.
#   Docs: docs/spark-farm.mdx
